# Angular Component Structure - MANDATORY RULES

## CRITICAL: Always Use External HTML Files

**MANDATORY RULE**: All Angular components MUST use external HTML template files (`.html`) instead of inline templates in the `template` property.

## Rules

1. **External Template Files**:
   - ALWAYS create a `.html` file for component templates
   - Use `templateUrl: './component-name.html'` instead of `template: \`...\``
   - The HTML file should be in the same directory as the component TypeScript file
   - Example: `retention.component.ts` → `retention.html`

2. **Minimal Styles in HTML**:
   - For minimal/simple styles (1-3 CSS properties), prefer inline styles directly in HTML using `style` attribute or Tailwind classes
   - Avoid creating a `styles` array in `@Component` decorator for minimal styling
   - Only use `styles` array or `styleUrls` when you have complex CSS (4+ properties, animations, pseudo-selectors, etc.)

3. **When to Use Inline Styles in HTML**:
   - Single property: `style="min-height: 400px"`
   - Simple Tailwind classes: `class="min-h-[400px]"`
   - Conditional styling: `[style.min-height.px]="400"`
   - These are preferred over component-level styles for minimal cases

4. **When to Use Component Styles**:
   - Complex CSS with multiple properties
   - CSS animations or transitions
   - Pseudo-selectors (`:hover`, `:focus`, etc.)
   - Media queries
   - CSS variables or complex selectors
   - When styles need to be scoped to the component

## Examples

### ✅ CORRECT:
```typescript
// retention.component.ts
@Component({
  selector: 'app-retention',
  templateUrl: './retention.html',
  // No styles array for minimal styling
})
```

```html
<!-- retention.html -->
<div class="retention-container min-h-[400px]">
  <!-- content -->
</div>
```

### ❌ WRONG:
```typescript
// retention.component.ts
@Component({
  selector: 'app-retention',
  template: `<div class="retention-container">...</div>`, // Inline template
  styles: [` // Minimal styles in component
    .retention-container {
      min-height: 400px;
    }
  `],
})
```

### ✅ CORRECT (Complex Styles):
```typescript
// complex.component.ts
@Component({
  selector: 'app-complex',
  templateUrl: './complex.html',
  styles: [`
    .complex-container {
      min-height: 400px;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
      animation: fadeIn 0.3s ease-in;
    }
    @keyframes fadeIn {
      from { opacity: 0; }
      to { opacity: 1; }
    }
    .complex-container:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
  `],
})
```

## File Structure

```
component-name/
  ├── component-name.component.ts  (TypeScript)
  ├── component-name.html           (Template - REQUIRED)
  └── component-name.component.scss (Styles - Optional, only if complex)
```

## Code Review Checklist

- [ ] Component uses `templateUrl` pointing to external `.html` file
- [ ] No inline `template` property in `@Component` decorator
- [ ] Minimal styles (1-3 properties) are in HTML using inline styles or Tailwind classes
- [ ] Complex styles (4+ properties, animations) use `styles` array or `styleUrls`
- [ ] HTML file exists in the same directory as component TypeScript file

**REMEMBER**: 
- Always create `.html` files for templates
- Prefer inline styles/Tailwind in HTML for minimal styling
- Use component styles only for complex CSS needs
